# Caddy is the only edge process in this stack now — it replaced nginx
# entirely (see server/Dockerfile's comment), so it does three things nginx
# used to split across nginx.conf + entrypoint.sh's htpasswd generation:
# TLS, Basic Auth, and reverse proxying, including the SSE run-progress
# stream. Caddy's reverse_proxy doesn't buffer by default the way nginx
# does, so unlike the old nginx.conf there's no separate location block or
# proxy_buffering/chunked_transfer_encoding tuning needed just for the SSE
# route (/api/run) — one reverse_proxy directive covers everything.
#
# Cert issuance: on first request, Caddy obtains a Let's Encrypt cert via
# the HTTP-01 challenge (needs ports 80+443 reachable from the internet and
# DNS already pointed at this box), then renews it automatically in the
# background for as long as this container runs. No certbot, no cron job.
#
# DOMAIN/ACME_EMAIL/BASIC_AUTH_* come from docker-compose.prod.yml's
# environment block, sourced from .env.production — see
# "Migrating to a new domain" in DEPLOYMENT.md if focusario.com ever
# changes.
#
# www.focusario.com redirects to the apex rather than serving a second
# copy — one canonical origin, one cert covering both names (Caddy issues
# a single cert listing both SANs automatically since both are declared
# below), no duplicated basicauth block to keep in sync.
#
# api.focusario.com is NOT wired up here yet — that CNAME exists in DNS
# but nothing serves it. The API is reachable at {$DOMAIN}/api/* today
# (FastAPI serves UI+API from one origin — see api/main.py). A dedicated
# api.focusario.com site block (its own reverse_proxy to api:8000, its
# own basicauth or a different auth scheme for programmatic/non-browser
# clients) is a deliberate later addition, not an oversight — add it here
# when there's an actual client that wants API access without the web UI
# wrapper, rather than standing up an unused second entry point now.
{
	email {$ACME_EMAIL}
}

www.{$DOMAIN} {
	redir https://{$DOMAIN}{uri} permanent
}

{$DOMAIN} {
	basicauth {
		{$BASIC_AUTH_USER} {$BASIC_AUTH_HASH}
	}

	reverse_proxy api:8000
}
